description:
Route every CLI test that plants, reads or corrupts lease storage through one test-support module, so the lease store layout is spelled once in the test tree.

## Background

CLI tests reach the claims store directly:

- `tests/cli_item_validate/validation_lease_tests.rs` (`write_claims_index`, a malformed index);
- `tests/cli_repo_workflow/claim_integration_tests.rs` (reads a lease from the index, removes the index's permissions, removes the index in recovery tests);
- `tests/cli_repo_workflow/external_data_root_tests.rs` (asserts `jit/claims.jsonl` exists under a data root outside every checkout);
- `tests/cli_issue/failure_probe_fixture.rs` (`malformed-claim-index`), with setup notes in `tests/cli_issue/failure_lever_registry.toml`;
- `tests/cli_issue/command_exit_code_projection_tests.rs` (corrupts the index).

Shared CLI test code lives in the `test-support` surface: `src/test_cli.rs`, `src/test_utils.rs`, `src/test_harness.rs`, declared in `src/lib.rs` under `#[cfg(any(test, feature = "test-support"))]` (`dev/TESTING.md`). Lease storage lives under `WorktreePaths::shared_jit`, which is `<common-dir>/jit` in primary, linked and external-data-root layouts, so a fixture cannot derive it as `root/.git/jit`.

## Success Criteria

- [hard] REQ-01: One `test-support` module takes `shared_jit` as input and plants a lease, reads a lease, names an issue's lease storage path and corrupts lease storage. The listed tests use it, and no CLI test names `claims.index.json` or `claims.jsonl` outside it.
- [hard] REQ-02: The listed tests pass unchanged in what they assert.
